ive contribution, referencing existing discussion, using facts, and state current recommendation.\n\nWe can either agree with current leading candidate (C) or propose alternative. We should consider all candidates. We have notes: Candidate B strong reliability and stress handling but nasty remarks. Candidate D strong responsibility but hot temper. Candidate A strong anticipation but unfriendly, unhealthy.\n\nWe might argue that while C has strengths, his communication and egocentric attitude are serious concerns for crew cooperation, which may outweigh his decision-making strengths. Perhaps Candidate B, despite some communication issues, is very conscientious and handles stress well, and his technical skills are good. However, B makes nasty remarks, which is also a crew cooperation issue.\n\nCandidate D takes responsibility seriously, concentrates, solves problems, but has hot temper and know-it-all attitude, also crew cooperation concerns.\n\nCandidate A has leadership and anticipation but unfriendly and unhealthy, also not open to new ideas.\n\nWe need to decide recommendation. Perhaps we could argue that Candidate B is the strongest overall because his conscientiousness (operational reliability) and stress handling are critical, and his technical skills are solid, while his communication issue (nasty remarks) is a concern but could be mitigated with training. Meanwhile C's egocentric and unwillingness to further education is more problematic for long-term development.\n\nThus we could shift vote to Candidate B. Provide evidence: \"very conscientious\", \"handles stress very well\", \"good at assessing weather conditions\", \"excellent computer skills\". Concern: \"makes nasty remarks about colleagues\". Argue that reliability and stress resilience are top criteria, and his strengths outweigh the communication issue, which can be addressed.\n\nWe must reference prior discussion: mention that others favor C for calmness and decision speed, but we think B's reliability and stress handling are more essential.\n\nThus our public message: agree that C's calmness is good, but raise concerns about crew cooperation and adaptability, and propose B as better overall.\n\nMetadata vote: Candidate B.\n\nLet's produce."}
